# Recipe for script/combat/pvp.razor. Build it with: node util/build-scripts.mjs
# Every setting of this loop: node util/build-scripts.mjs --settings recipe/pvp-recipe.razor
# @ output script/combat/pvp.razor


# ========================================================================================
# @ header
# ========================================================================================

# Shared field PvP self-sustain: opening self TK, recovery, RA, Reflect, Protection and remembered hands.
# Needs: the heal pot, reflect and teleki, me bars. Hold the weapon to remember before Play.
# Turn it on when a PvP fight starts. All offense stays manual: attack spells, offensive TK, explosion potions,
# pets, targeting and melee requests. The script never cuts a manual cast or cursor.
# No start 4 lines (conventions 02.D, config__clear_at_start 0): a manual cursor or cast held at Play is kept.
# Each hand is remembered before the opening cast. Re-arm only without casting, a cursor or an item queue.
# Design: content/public/loops/pvp.md. In-game checks: content/public/questions/open-items.md part 10.
#
# Shape
#   Each block reads the live state and acts on the spot, the way bard-necro-enhanced and
#   lumberjack-enhanced do. No block hands a decision to a later one. Item uses go through
#   Razor's object delay queue, and every block waits while that queue is busy. A cast block
#   waits out its own cast in a for 60 poll, so the next block sees casting end.
#
# Input rules (wiki Combat Overview, content/public/game/pvp.md part 5.B)
#   Potions and the pouch are instant and go out while a spell is casting.
#   Drinking with a finished precast cursor in hand cancels that spell, so a potion or a
#   bandage waits while any cursor is held. Agents and buffs need no cast and no cursor.
#   Only our own buff cast is cut, at config__buff_max_loss, so the next pass can heal.
#   No walk guard (config__walk_guard 0): in a fight there is no better moment to wait for.
#
# Cost (content/public/scripting/razor.md part 6)
#   findtype is the most expensive statement. Opening TK checks just its two reagents.
#   Other reagents are read in REAGENTS every
#   interval__reagents and right after a "More reagents are needed" refusal, and the cast
#   blocks read the flags. Potions are looked up only inside a block that already needs one.


# ========================================================================================
# @ blocks
#
#   One box per block, in the order the blocks run, base first. The builder writes the box.
#   Yours are the "> " lines in it (a note on the block, or under a setting the reason for
#   its value) and the @setvar! lines under it. Write a new @setvar! line under any box, its
#   reason as a "#" line right above it: the builder moves both to the box it belongs to.
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use base
#
#   The frame of every loop and routine. Every recipe lists it first.
#
#   clear_at_start (default 1)
#      What Play does first (conventions 02.D).
#        0  nothing: a cursor or a cast the player holds at Play is kept
#        1  clear the client queues, the journal and the ignore list
#      > A manual cursor or cast held at Play is kept (conventions 02.D).
#
#   walk_guard (default 1)
#      Our casts and the walk bar.
#        0  cast while walking, for a fight where there is no better moment to wait for
#        1  wait while the walk bar runs, so a step does not break the cast
#      Greater Heal at the emergency line goes out in either (recovery/heal).
#      Read by recovery/cure, recovery/light-heal, buff/spells.
#      > pvp casts while walking: in a fight there is no better moment to wait for.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__clear_at_start 0
@setvar! config__walk_guard 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use fight/remember-hands
#
#   Records the current hand pair before another block can cast and drop its weapon.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use buff/self-telekinesis
#
#   Tries defensive Telekinesis on yourself once in the first free cast window after Play.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use magery/reagents
#
#   Reagent flags for the Magery casts, the mana per circle and the shared cast settings.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ when paralyzed or poisoned or diffhits > 0
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/cure
#
#   The trapped pouch while paralyzed, else a cure potion or the Smart Heal/Cure agent.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/heal
#
#   Heal potion at heal_hits, else Greater Heal at emergency_hits.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/bandage
#
#   Self bandage while hurt or poisoned, never over a running one.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/light-heal
#
#   The light Heal agent: the bandage stand-in, or beside them with use_light_heal 1.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ========================================================================================
# @ end
# ========================================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use recovery/refresh
#
#   Total Refresh at or below refresh_stam.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use buff/potions
#
#   Strength and Agility by stat value, Magic Resist by its icon, while fighting.
#
#   str_potion (default 120, the same value)
#      STR with the Greater Strength potion on: your base plus 20. Below it the potion is
#      drunk, and 0 turns it off. Bless and the Strength spell, ours or an ally's, show
#      the same icon as the potion but add less than its 20, so the stat tells them apart.
#      > The loop is shared, so set this for the character that runs it.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__str_potion 120

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use buff/spells
#
#   Reactive Armor, then Magic Reflection, whenever one is missing.
#
#   use_reactive_armor (default 1, the same value)
#      1 keeps Reactive Armor up.
#
#   use_magic_reflect (default 1, the same value)
#      1 keeps Magic Reflection up.
#
#   use_protection (default 0)
#      1 keeps Protection on yourself, in a fight too. Follows warmode_is_manual, like
#      Reactive Armor and Magic Reflection. Arch Protection shows the same Protection
#      icon, so one of the two is enough.
#      > Keep the three defensive buffs up during a field fight, including in warmode.
#
#   use_bless (default 0, the same value)
#      1 keeps Bless on yourself, and Arch Protection on you and the followers around you,
#      while no enemy is engaged (var__fighting 0) and warmode is off. Both open a cursor
#      answered with yourself, Bless a beneficial one and Arch Protection a neutral one, so
#      they never take a cast from a fight.
#
#   use_arch_protection (default 0, the same value)
#      1 keeps Bless on yourself, and Arch Protection on you and the followers around you,
#      while no enemy is engaged (var__fighting 0) and warmode is off. Both open a cursor
#      answered with yourself, Bless a beneficial one and Arch Protection a neutral one, so
#      they never take a cast from a fight.
#
#   buff_max_loss (default 35, the same value)
#      Missing hit points at which buffs are not started, and cut mid cast.
#      > Keep this equal to config__emergency_hits.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__use_reactive_armor 1
@setvar! config__use_magic_reflect 1
@setvar! config__use_protection 1
@setvar! config__use_bless 0
@setvar! config__use_arch_protection 0
@setvar! config__buff_max_loss 35

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ use fight/rearm
#
#   Re-arms what each hand held, out of the backpack, when a cast or a disarm empties it.
#
#   rearm_follow_hands (default 0)
#      What to remember when equipment changes.
#        0  remember each hand independently
#        1  adopt both current hands at Play and when a new held item is seen. Forget an
#           empty opposite hand in that case. If both hands are empty, keep the memory
#           so a cast or disarm can still be repaired
#      Also read by fight/remember-hands.
#      > Follow the currently chosen hands, including a manual one-handed or two-handed swap.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__rearm_follow_hands 1


# ========================================================================================
# @ state
# ========================================================================================

# pvp is always in a fight, so the stat potions are kept up the whole time.
@setvar! var__fighting 1


# ========================================================================================
# @ setup
# ========================================================================================

overhead "[ pvp, on ]" 290
if config__sysmsg = 1
    sysmsg "PvP sustain v10 loaded. Opening self TK, defensive buffs, remembered hands." 88
endif
